# Mobile-browser first

The shipped experience is a mobile browser: iPhone Safari, iOS Chrome, and Android Chrome and Safari. Desktop browsers are a secondary target.

When building or changing UI, layout, styling, interaction, or rendered data:

1. Design and implement for a phone viewport first (narrow width, touch input, on-screen keyboard, safe areas).
2. Then adapt the same UI so it still works on desktop browsers.
3. Prefer CSS that starts from the small screen and adds desktop styles with min-width media queries.
4. Use touch-friendly targets, avoid hover-only actions, and account for mobile browser chrome (address bar, safe-area insets, 100vh quirks).
5. Verify behavior on a phone-sized viewport before treating a desktop layout as done.
